Algorithm 
Start the program.
Read the number of vertices and edges.
Create an adjacency list to represent the graph.
Enter the paths connecting the vertices.
Accept the starting vertex from the user.
Apply DFS and display the traversal order.
Apply BFS using a queue and display the traversal order.
Mark all vertices visited during BFS as reachable.
Count the reachable vertices and display their BFS levels.
Display the vertices that are unreachable from the starting vertex.
Stop the program.
